          "label": "what it is",
          "labelStyle": "label",
          "value": "truth is in shades, not black and white. Introducing a word cuts a continuous reality into a shape; the moment a framework names something, it looks like it's claiming one side. Some apparent conflicts are artifacts of that. She digests conflicts herself; Claude's job is to present what each system says, side by side. `[hers]`",
